@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# In-place source upgrade applicability
+
+Target installed from public VCS at `909977b762ff08f823be1e2c16a4dbb704e4f93a`, Contract 18/Profile 4. Both Composer source and dist references are pinned; this is source evaluation, not package publication evidence. The public Alpha 7 app and subsequent search feature remain the same retained application. `docs/lifecycle-plan.md` remains the frozen plan.
+
+Derived from the INSTALLED `vendor/phpthis/framework/docs/consumer-contract-upgrades.md`, Contract 14–18; current contract/map, errors and request-handling guide supply the entered requirements.
+
+| Change | Applicability and retained repair/evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| 14: raw target/path bytes | Literal route declarations and fixtures contained no newly excluded bytes. `tests/compatibility.php` proves NUL/tab/0x1f/space/DEL in query suffix stop before handler work, direct Request/Route reject without echo, and existing percent/slash/dot/backslash/high bytes remain unchanged. Real loopback HTTP preserves ordinary paths/search; no proxy or alternate adapter claim. |
+| 15 / PHT008 | Every existing statement already uses distinct placeholder occurrences, as Alpha 7 prose required. Installed checker and original SQL-looking data/1-query tests pass. No intentional duplicate-placeholder baseline or binding rewrite. Profile markers move 3 to 4. |
+| 16: source discovery | Application-owned checked-in files are readable regular files/directories; PHP entrypoints use .php, Python files are decisively non-PHP. No app symlinks or extensionless PHP adopted. The transient HTTP fixture links only its vendor dependency boundary; it is outside the checked application tree. Inventory plus complete checker pass retained by campaign. |
+| 17: pending output | Only public/index.php emits. Existing bootstrap/handlers print no pre-emitter bytes. Existing CLI capture begins empty. New real-controller child tests prove empty-buffer success, top/lower pending-byte rejection, unchanged buffer contents/depth and zero fallback on responseStarted=true. Tests clean buffers only after assertions. Custom handlers/files/proxies are not adopted. |
+| 18: outer HTTP boundary | APPLICABLE COMPATIBILITY REPAIR. First installed-target complete gate passed static and existing behavior but failed new real-SAPI missing-fixture test: expected exact generic body, got empty body. Tag upgrade-red is a failed checkpoint. Move ordinary autoload/generic construction before one Throwable catch; retain generic before one safe-class event attempt; keep emission catch separate. No context/skeleton replacement. |
+| 18: disclosure selection/details | Deliberately code-owned GENERIC, no inputs or renderer. Details selection, paired-input validation, message allowlists and renderer/truncation branches are not adopted and not claimed tested. Tests prove supplied debug/profile/query/header hints cannot enable details. |
+| 18: native SAPI/outer event | PHP built-in SAPI assertions prove all E_ALL bits, display/startup display off, log_errors on to a private scratch destination, and exception arguments omitted. Actual original bootstrap missing its fixture, controlled bootstrap failure, anonymous class redaction and disabled error_log prove exact generic response/event and event failure isolation. Earlier autoload/generic-setup failure, uncatchable termination and lost-response ownership remain outside this app boundary. |
+
+No runtime schema, named policy, data, user input, transaction, pagination, or dependency other than phpthis/framework is changed by this upgrade. Existing app-owned context is edited at the specific version/HTTP concerns. Unknown coordinator failures and starter emission fallback tests remain intact. All valid checkpoints require the entire zero-argument `composer check`.
